Locally authored vz concurrent-exec correction for pinned youki 0.7.0.
Not an upstream-reviewed backport. Apply AFTER every other local patch.

A tenant (exec) invocation named its notify socket from a single `fastrand`
draw and accepted the name if no file held it yet. `fastrand`'s global
generator seeds itself from a hash of `Instant::now()` and the thread id, with
no OS entropy, so two runtime processes started in the same instant - a
container healthcheck and a `docker exec`, say - seed identically, draw
identically, both find the name free, and the one that binds second fails with
EADDRINUSE, reported as "failed to bind notify socket: tenant-notify-<hex>.sock".
Measured on this pinned binary at 21 failures in 480 execs (8-way) with the
container directory emptied between rounds, so nothing but a concurrent
collision could produce them.

The name now carries the reserving process's id, which two live invocations
cannot share, and reservation is the bind itself rather than an existence test
followed by a later bind, so no window remains between the two. The socket is
also removed once the start notification has been delivered; it used to be left
behind, one dead socket per exec for the lifetime of the container. The console
socket link of an exec gets the same treatment, its `symlink(2)` already being
atomic. A failed bind no longer leaves the process parked in the container
directory, where a later relative path would resolve against the wrong root.

